WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.712 --> 00:00:15.201
The looked at Fix in surprise and said, "There's a thief on board the Mongolia?

2
00:00:15.762 --> 00:00:16.522
Are you certain?"

3
00:00:16.542 --> 00:00:19.744
"Consul, I have no doubt.

4
00:00:20.905 --> 00:00:24.047
I have spotted my man," said Fix with conviction.

5
00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:30.732
"He passes himself off as an eccentric, rich man who is going around the world in eighty days.

6
00:00:32.224 --> 00:00:35.906
When he arrives to have his passport stamped, you must hold him here!"

7
00:00:35.926 --> 00:00:40.288
"He is coming to have a visa entered in his passport?"

8
00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:41.629
asked the consul.

9
00:00:41.649 --> 00:00:47.252
"Yes, but I hope you will not issue the visa," said Fix.

10
00:00:48.593 --> 00:00:49.013
"Why not?

11
00:00:49.633 --> 00:00:52.055
If the passport is genuine, I have no right to refuse."

12
00:00:52.075 --> 00:00:56.937
"Criminals such as this man use passports to flee the law.

13
00:00:57.918 --> 00:00:58.978
You must keep him here!"

14
00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.500
replied Fix, his frustration growing.

15
00:01:02.932 --> 00:01:06.674
"I cannot hold a man, no matter how sure you are of his guilt, without a warrant.

16
00:01:08.395 --> 00:01:11.577
Surely you are aware of that," replied the consul, shaking his head.

17
00:01:11.597 --> 00:01:13.138
"Perhaps this Mr.

18
00:01:13.178 --> 00:01:16.520
Fogg won't even come here if he is indeed the person you suppose him to be.

19
00:01:16.540 --> 00:01:20.162
A robber doesn't like to leave traces of his flight behind him, you know.

20
00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:24.944
Besides, he is not obligated to have his passport stamped anyway."

21
00:01:24.965 --> 00:01:30.848
"If he is as shrewd as I think he is, consul, he will—" began Fix.

22
00:01:32.096 --> 00:01:34.398
But before he could finish, someone knocked on the door.

23
00:01:36.299 --> 00:01:41.442
Fix quickly hid himself in a corner of the room as Passepartout and his master entered the office.

24
00:01:42.683 --> 00:01:45.805
From his hiding place, Fix observed as the consul took Mr.

25
00:01:45.845 --> 00:01:47.867
Fogg's documents and read them carefully.

26
00:01:47.887 --> 00:01:50.668
"You are Mr.

27
00:01:50.728 --> 00:01:51.509
Phileas Fogg?"

28
00:01:51.989 --> 00:01:52.870
asked the consul.

29
00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.512
"I am," said Fogg.

30
00:01:55.532 --> 00:01:57.953
"And this is your servant?"

31
00:01:58.434 --> 00:01:59.294
asked the consul.

32
00:01:59.314 --> 00:02:01.856
"He is," said Fogg.

33
00:02:02.508 --> 00:02:04.089
"A Frenchman named Passepartout."

34
00:02:04.109 --> 00:02:06.030
"You are from London?"

35
00:02:06.451 --> 00:02:07.311
asked the consul.

36
00:02:07.331 --> 00:02:09.072
"Yes," said Fogg.

37
00:02:09.093 --> 00:02:12.395
"And you are going asked the consul.

38
00:02:12.415 --> 00:02:14.796
"To Bombay," replied Mr.

39
00:02:14.836 --> 00:02:17.898
Fogg. "Very good, sir," said the consul.

40
00:02:17.918 --> 00:02:21.661
"You know that no passport is required and a visa would be meaningless?"

41
00:02:21.681 --> 00:02:25.363
"I know it, sir," replied Phileas Fogg.

42
00:02:25.383 --> 00:02:29.986
"But I wish to prove, by your visa, that I traveled via Suez."

43
00:02:31.347 --> 00:02:32.028
"Very well, sir."

44
00:02:33.228 --> 00:02:37.489
The consul proceeded to sign and date the passport, and then added his official seal.

45
00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:42.471
Mr. Fogg paid the fee, bowed, and went out, followed by Passepartout.

46
00:02:44.391 --> 00:02:46.492
After leaving the consul's office, Mr.

47
00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:49.793
Fogg returned to the dock and gave some instructions to Passepartout.

48
00:02:51.853 --> 00:02:55.834
Then he made his way to his cabin on the Mongolia and picked up his travel journal.

49
00:02:57.175 --> 00:03:01.156
In this journal a detailed itinerary listed all the major stopping points on Mr.

50
00:03:01.176 --> 00:03:12.561
Fogg's route: Paris, Brindisi, Suez, Bombay, Calcutta, Singapore, Hong Kong, Yokohama, San Francisco, New York, and finally London.

51
00:03:13.942 --> 00:03:18.004
Next to each was written the expected day and time of arrival with a space for noting the

52
00:03:18.124 --> 00:03:20.705
actual arrival time and the hours gained or lost.

53
00:03:22.026 --> 00:03:22.987
As a result Mr.

54
00:03:23.027 --> 00:03:26.368
Fogg always knew whether he was behind or in advance of his schedule.

55
00:03:27.589 --> 00:03:34.592
He added his newest entry: Reached Suez Wednesday, October 9, at 11:00 a.m.

56
00:03:34.612 --> 00:03:38.374
Total of hours spent: 158; or in days: six and a half.

57
00:03:39.974 --> 00:03:44.416
As Fogg closed his journal and put away his pen, he observed that he had neither gained nor

58
00:03:44.476 --> 00:03:45.097
lost time.

59
00:03:46.357 --> 00:03:50.999
He sat down quietly to eat breakfast in his cabin, never once thinking of visiting the town.

60
00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:53.700
After seeing Mr.

61
00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:57.001
Fogg in person, Fix was convinced that Fogg was the culprit.

62
00:03:58.382 --> 00:04:00.523
Fogg fit the description of the robber perfectly.

63
00:04:00.543 --> 00:04:04.701
"Everything adds up," Fix said to himself.

64
00:04:04.721 --> 00:04:13.084
"His leaving London so quickly, his hiring a new servant the very same day It's all very suspicious."

65
00:04:14.705 --> 00:04:17.026
Fix quickly decided that he must follow Mr.

66
00:04:17.066 --> 00:04:22.488
Fogg. It was his duty, after all, and the reward for catching such a cunning criminal as this

67
00:04:22.568 --> 00:04:24.269
supposed gentleman would be his.

68
00:04:25.709 --> 00:04:27.030
Fix turned to the consul.

69
00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:29.331
"I must leave at once.

70
00:04:29.751 --> 00:04:31.712
I am going to telegraph the police in London.

71
00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.501
I must follow this man!"

72
00:04:34.961 --> 00:04:35.401
he said.

73
00:04:36.301 --> 00:04:38.802
The detective thanked the consul for his help and left.

74
00:04:40.183 --> 00:04:45.225
Fix went immediately to the telegraph office and sent the following wire: Suez to London.

75
00:04:46.666 --> 00:04:49.207
Rowan, Commissioner of Police, Scotland Yard.

76
00:04:49.867 --> 00:04:51.968
I've found the bank robber, Phileas Fogg.

77
00:04:52.668 --> 00:04:54.889
Send an arrest warrant to Bombay without delay.

78
00:04:55.609 --> 00:04:56.770
Fix, Detective.

79
00:04:57.970 --> 00:05:02.492
A quarter of an hour later, with a small bag in his hand, Fix boarded the Mongolia.

80
00:05:06.412 --> 00:05:09.113
During our journey it's my job to keep track of Mr.

81
00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:09.973
Fogg's passport.

82
00:05:10.574 --> 00:05:12.655
If I lose it, I will be in big trouble!

83
00:05:13.955 --> 00:05:16.656
Whenever you travel abroad, you must bring a passport with you.

84
00:05:18.177 --> 00:05:22.138
A passport is a document issued by your country for the purpose of overseas travel.

85
00:05:23.379 --> 00:05:27.921
The word "passport" most likely comes from the medieval word for the gate, or porte, of a city.

86
00:05:29.381 --> 00:05:32.923
Notice my name, Passepartout, looks a lot like the word "passport."

87
00:05:33.863 --> 00:05:35.764
Hmm that's a funny coincidence, isn't it!

88
00:05:37.008 --> 00:05:41.512
Foreign governments use passports to identify who is arriving in, or leaving, their country.

89
00:05:43.073 --> 00:05:47.877
When you arrive in a foreign country, you must obtain a visa, which gives you permission to enter

90
00:05:47.917 --> 00:05:48.377
the country.

91
00:05:48.998 --> 00:05:52.341
The visa is either stamped into or attached to your passport.

92
00:05:53.521 --> 00:05:55.483
I have to admit, I was a little worried that Mr.

93
00:05:55.523 --> 00:05:59.006
Fogg's passport wouldn't have enough pages for all the countries we were going to visit.

94
00:06:00.067 --> 00:06:03.329
If he did run out, perhaps the visas could be stamped onto his forehead.

95
00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:05.571
Ha-ha! Don't tell Mr.

96
00:06:05.591 --> 00:06:06.332
Fogg I said that!
